@startuml send-claim-invitation-sequence
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
title Figure 4.3.4.2.1 Send Claim Invitation Sequence Diagram
hide footbox
autonumber
actor Brand
participant "Web Client" as Web
participant CreatorInvitationController as API
participant CreatorInvitationService as Service
participant CreatorInvitationRepository as Repo
participant ClaimEmailOutboxService as Outbox
participant ClaimEmailDispatch as Dispatch
participant ClaimEmailWorker as Worker
Brand -> Web : invite a Creator to claim a channel
Web -> API : POST /api/v1/creators/{id}/invite
activate API
API -> Service : sendInvitation(creatorId, email, brandId, campaignId)
activate Service
alt <U+005B>Brand authority or campaign ownership check fails<U+005D>
  Service --> API : authorization or lookup error
else <U+005B>authorized Brand<U+005D>
  alt <U+005B>channel already owned or live claim invitation exists<U+005D>
    Service --> API : ownership or pending invitation conflict
  else <U+005B>channel eligible and email delivery configured<U+005D>
    Service -> Repo : save(invitation) with token hash and expiry
    Service -> Outbox : enqueue(saved, claimUrl)
    Outbox --> Service : email job persisted in current transaction
    Service --> API : InvitationResponse with emailStatus QUEUED
  else <U+005B>email delivery or claim URL configuration invalid<U+005D>
    Service --> API : configuration error
  end
end
deactivate Service
API --> Web : invitation result or mapped error
deactivate API
opt <U+005B>invitation and email job transaction committed<U+005D>
  Dispatch ->> Worker : sendAsync(jobId)
end
@enduml
